    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Road to Rouen is the fifth studio album by Supergrass, released in 2005 on Parlophone. It marked a notable stylistic shift for the band: instead of the brisk, hook-heavy Britpop that made them famous, the album leans toward a more reflective, melodic rock sound with longer songs, softer textures, and a restrained, autumnal atmosphere.\n\nRecorded in Rouen, France, the album’s title nods both to that location and to the Ramones’ Road to Ruin. It was widely seen as one of Supergrass’s most mature and critically respected records, praised for its emotional depth and subtle arrangements on songs such as “Low C,” “Fin,” and “St. Petersburg.”",
